+{"step":"spec-19082","answer":{"data":{"repository":{"pullRequest":{"body":"Closes #19063\n\n## Summary\n\nThe comment lint's CI re-run was a hand-copied README recipe, and this repository ran its own GitHub-only wrapper (`scripts/check-comment-lint.sh`, keyed on `GITHUB_EVENT_NAME`, `HEAD_SHA` and `BASE_REF`). This ships one CI-neutral script in the plugin and a guided `/code-tidying:setup apply install-ci` that discovers the repository's CI system and proposes the step in that system's own format, with no CI system as a default and no vendor template, as the owner asked on 2026-11-25.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `plugins/code-tidying/git-hooks/comment-lint-ci.sh <head> <base>`: both commits as arguments, no vendor variable. Adds a detached worktree at the head without checking files out (the lint reads the index, so the repository's files never land on disk), soft-resets to the merge base, restores `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and the home's `code-tidying.yaml`/`code-tidying.local.yaml` from the merge base, runs `comment-lint.sh` from beside itself, removes the worktree; exits with the lint's status, 2 on usage. Listed as an asset in `entries.json`, so a shared hook install commits it under `.githooks/code-tidying/` where a consumer's CI can call it.\n- `plugins/code-tidying/scripts/comment-lint-ci-scan.py`: read-only JSON for the setup agent: CI systems found by their configuration files (GitHub Actions, Azure Pipelines, GitLab CI, Jenkins, CircleCI, Bitbucket and others), task-runner files, which files name `python3`/pygments, callers of the script (arguments parsed through template expressions and continued lines) or of the older recipe, and `decisions[]` (`no-ci-system`, `several-systems`, `no-caller`, `recipe-caller`, `drift`, `unparsed`, `unreached-caller`, `missing-tool`), mirroring the installer's plan shape. A commented-out line is never a caller, and a caller in a make, task or just target counts only when an uncommented CI line runs that target; otherwise it is `unreached-caller` (not installed).\n- Setup skill: new `apply install-ci` (discover, stop when present, ask only what discovery leaves open, propose in the system's format and the repository's conventions, write only on a yes, print for a system it cannot write); `check` step 10 reports the caller, drift and `unreached-caller` as a FAIL, the recipe as INFO. New `reference/ci-systems.md`: what the step does in any system, where the script comes from, and an instruction to read the named system's own documentation at run time. It links no vendor page: docs/plugin-philosophy.md \"No ecosystem-specific examples\" bars \"a link to one tool's documentation\" in a shipped reference file and makes no exception for a side-by-side list, so the vendor table was removed. The `no-ci-rerun` decision now offers `apply install-ci`.\n- This repository: `pr-require-checks.yml`'s comment-lint step calls the shipped script (`\"$HEAD_SHA\" \"origin/$BASE_REF\"`, pull_request only, as before); `scripts/check-comment-lint.sh` and its test are deleted (its cases moved to `comment-lint-ci.test.sh`); the `check-script-contract` registry row and `check-affected.sh`'s description follow.\n- README: the recipe is replaced by how `apply install-ci` works and the script's interface. Changelog fragment `bump: minor`. No default or setting changed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `plugins/code-tidying/git-hooks/comment-lint-ci.test.sh`: 23 checks pass, every case of the deleted `check-comment-lint.test.sh` (base level wins, home rename, planted symlink, base moving ahead) plus a flat copy laid out like an installed hook, an ADR pointer with no files checked out, and the usage errors.\n- `test_comment_lint_ci_scan.py`: 25 tests pass (vendor detection, template expressions, continued lines, Groovy quoting, drift, recipe callers, missing tool, commented-out callers, and reach: the review repro of a `.gitlab-ci.yml` running only `make test` beside a Makefile `comment-lint` target reports `unreached-caller`; make, just and task targets a CI line runs are reached).\n- `comment-lint.test.sh` (72), `lib/git-hooks/sh-entries.test.sh` (254; caught a bare `bash` call in the new asset, fixed), `lefthook-remote.test.sh`, `install.test.sh`, `check-affected*.test.sh`: pass on the merged head.\n- The 61 suites that read `pr-require-checks.yml`: 57 pass; `run-hygiene-gate.test.sh` and `ci-test-node-stop-commands.test.sh` pass when rerun with a `python3` that has PyYAML; `callers.test.mjs` and `admit.test.mjs` could not load `ajv`/`yaml` (no `node_modules` in this worktree), left to CI. `check-script-contract.test.sh` fails only its `check-html-assets` rows for the same missing `node_modules`.\n- Dogfood: `bash plugins/code-tidying/git-hooks/comment-lint-ci.sh HEAD origin/main` on this branch exits 0; the scan on this repository reports one `script` caller, `pr-require-checks.yml`, args `$HEAD_SHA origin/$BASE_REF`, no drift.\n- `scripts/check-changed-skills.sh origin/main`: PASS (5 size warnings; the body was already over the router cap before this change, the procedure moved to `actions/install-ci.md`). `scripts/check-changelog-fragments.sh --check-required origin/main`: pass.\n\n## Related\n\n- `scripts/check-affected.sh` keeps its own local variant of the merge-base lint (a scratch repository over alternates), unchanged here.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n","lastEditedAt":"2026-11-25T14:55:20Z","closingIssuesReferences":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"number":19063,"repository":{"nameWithOwner":"melodic-software/claude-code-plugins"}}]},"renames":{"nodes":[],"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":null}}}}}}}
