+[{"body":"\u003c!-- claude-lane intake-triage --\u003e\n\nSize: Large\nComplexity: Medium\nUncertainty: Knowable\nFlags: none\nBlocked by: none\nBlast radius: a new markdown map under docs/conventions/; read by maintainers and lane authors, no workflow or code change.\nReversible: yes; revert the committed document.\nClaims checked:\n1. `docs/conventions/pr-pipeline.yaml` exists: held, `docs/conventions/pr-pipeline.yaml`.\n2. Workflows under `.github/workflows/` number in the low-to-mid 40s (issue says 43): held, 44 `.yml` files found by glob in `.github/workflows/`.\nOpen questions: none\n\n\u003e **Decision recorded.** Start this issue on the refinement's recommendations (owner, in session 2026-11-25T03:15Z, verbatim: `/session-flow:go-with-recommendations`, accepting \"(A) start it on the refinement's recommendations\").\n\u003e\n\u003e 1. Inputs: build the first map from the repository's workflows, actions and plugin inventory. Transcript and per-run measurements are a follow-up item with named data sources.\n\u003e 2. Location: a markdown document under `docs/conventions/`, beside the loop-lane convention, one table row per task.\n\u003e 3. Simplify pass: a map entry stating the chosen placement and its reason; its build is a separate issue.\n\u003e 4. UI question: the run records a provisional answer with its evidence; the owner confirms it later.\n\u003e 5. Criteria:\n\u003e\n\u003e - [ ] A lifecycle map document is committed under `docs/conventions/`, one table row per automated task, each row giving run shape (standalone or a step in an existing run), owning component (tracker, git host, runner, orchestrator or observability), trigger, inputs and outputs.\n\u003e - [ ] Every plugin in the repository's plugin inventory and every workflow under `.github/workflows/` is placed on the map or listed as not an automated task.\n\u003e - [ ] The map has a simplify-pass entry that states its placement and the reason, marked as built separately.\n\u003e - [ ] The map