be fixed before a run starts.\n   RECOMMENDED: Four items: map document committed with all five fields per task; every plugin in the inventory placed; simplify-pass entry with placement reasoning; UI question answer recorded in the map. Basis: judgment\n\n**Sources read**\n\n- .base/docs/conventions/loop-lane/README.md: existing lane convention, a likely neighbor for the map\n- .base/docs/contracts/lane-transcripts/README.md: contract for lane transcripts, a possible research input\n- .base/plugins/source-control/skills/pull-request/reference/prep.md: mentions simplify, relevant to the first map item\n\nTo answer, post a comment that starts with this line:\n\n```\n**Decision recorded.** \u003canswer\u003e\n```\n\n\u003csub\u003eAutomated refinement by the lanes App. Answer with a comment whose first line is `**Decision recorded.**`.\u003c/sub\u003e","html_url":"https://github.com/melodic-software/claude-code-plugins/issues/17133#issuecomment-6977730141","user":{"id":337595936,"login":"melodic-automation-lanes[bot]","type":"Bot"}},{"body":"**Decision recorded.** Start this issue on the refinement's recommendations (owner, in session 2026-11-25T03:15Z, verbatim: `/session-flow:go-with-recommendations`, accepting \"(A) start it on the refinement's recommendations\").\n\n1. Inputs: build the first map from the repository's workflows, actions and plugin inventory. Transcript and per-run measurements are a follow-up item with named data sources.\n2. Location: a markdown document under `docs/conventions/`, beside the loop-lane convention, one table row per task.\n3. Simplify pass: a map entry stating the chosen placement and its reason; its build is a separate issue.\n4. UI question: the run records a provisional answer with its evidence; the owner confirms it later.\n5. Criteria:\n\n- [ ] A lifecycle map document is committed under `docs/conventions/`, one table row per automated task, each row giving run shape (standalone or a step in an existing run), owning component (